From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The boxes' panel: its edges' stripes clear (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The panel of the Pokémon looked at has the PC's stripes drawn into its
edges (its palette's colours 10 and 14), where the stripes are behind
it on the DS. At the wider screen's left edge, beside the divider, they
showed as cyan and mint lines over it, whenever something was drawn
into the panel (a Pokémon's name, the party's tray opened). They are
shown clear now (WIDE_CLEAR: a new part for the port), so the stripes
behind show through as on the DS.
---
 include/port_wide_layout.h                | 5 +++++
 src/applications/pc_boxes/ov19_021D79F8.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/port_wide_layout.h b/include/port_wide_layout.h
index 00b9700f..111ea269 100644
--- a/include/port_wide_layout.h
+++ b/include/port_wide_layout.h
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@
 //     the wide art folder; nothing if it isn't there) with BG bg, in front
 //     of that BG's pixels: its top-left at the DS's x, y (anywhere on the
 //     wider screen), turned angle degrees clockwise about its middle.
+//   WIDE_CLEAR: the BG's colours of palette pal whose indices are bits of
+//     mask (bit i: index i; a 16-colour BG) shown clear, all over the BG:
+//     a panel's background drawn into its edges (the stripes behind the
+//     boxes' panel), so what's behind the BG shows there, as it did.
 // WIDE_SCREEN_COLUMNS with a part's BGs: its x0..x1-1 are columns of the
 // DS's screen, not of the BG's picture: they stay put as the BG scrolls
 // (a WIDE_FILL's col is still the picture's).
@@ -50,6 +54,7 @@ extern void NitroPort_WindowFramed(const void *window, int frame);
 #define WIDE_OBJS_STRETCH(top, bottom, x0, x1, dx) { 3, 0, (top), (bottom), (x0), (x1), (dx), 1 }
 #define WIDE_SHIFT3D(dx)                          { 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, (dx), 0 }
 #define WIDE_PICTURE(bg, picture, x, y, angle)    { 5, WIDE_BG(bg), (y), (y) + 1, (x), (x) + 1, (angle), (picture) }
+#define WIDE_CLEAR(bg, pal, mask)                 { 6, WIDE_BG(bg), 0, 1, 0, 1, (pal), (mask) }
 
 // The pictures (their files: <name>.png; the port's numbers, in
 // 3ds_port/nitro/include/nitro_port_wide.h, are the same).
diff --git a/src/applications/pc_boxes/ov19_021D79F8.c b/src/applications/pc_boxes/ov19_021D79F8.c
index 742f4396..511408a7 100644
--- a/src/applications/pc_boxes/ov19_021D79F8.c
+++ b/src/applications/pc_boxes/ov19_021D79F8.c
@@ -135,6 +135,10 @@ static void BoxWide_Apply(void)
         WIDE_OBJS(160, 256, -64, 108, -32),
         WIDE_OBJS(160, 256, 108, 400, 32),
         WIDE_SHIFT3D(-32),
+        // The panel's edges have the stripes behind it drawn in (its
+        // palette's 10 and 14): moved to the screen's edge, beside the
+        // divider, they were lines over it; clear, the stripes show through.
+        WIDE_CLEAR(2, 1, (1 << 10) | (1 << 14)),
         WIDE_PICTURE(3, WIDE_PICTURE_PC_BOXES_DIVIDER, 56, 0, 0), // (behind the panel's edge)
         WIDE_PICTURE(3, WIDE_PICTURE_PC_BOXES_BALL, 70, 75, 0),
     };
